    "id": "detection-pipeline",
    "caption": "From event to action: sources emit structured events, agents ship them off the host within seconds to storage the sources cannot alter, detections turn matching events into alerts with runbooks, and emulated attacks continuously prove the whole chain still fires.",
    "alt": "Sources on the left: identity provider, cloud audit trail, hosts, applications and Kubernetes. Agents forward their events to central write-once storage in a separate administrative boundary. A detection engine runs Sigma-style rules over the stored events and produces alerts that carry a runbook and enrichment. Alerts go to an on-call analyst or to an automated first response. An adversary emulation tool injects known techniques at the sources and checks that alerts appear, feeding gaps back into the detection backlog.",
